static const z_t84_t _zs257 = { .data = _zs257_d, .size = 220 };
static const char _zs258_d[] = "ownership error\n\nA value's ownership was used incorrectly: used after a take/move, a borrow outliving its lock, a reftype aliased while locked, or a reassignment in another mode than the name was bound with -- an owned name takes an owned value (`x = d.take`), a borrow is re-pointed (`b = d`). See docs/ownership.";
